WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
There's like all these stigmas
and kind of bad stereotypes

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.000
attached to strippers and dancers.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.920
I remember asking one of them,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.107
kind of a provocative question, like,

00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:13.347
"Do you ever go home with people
that you meet in the club?

00:00:13.347 --> 00:00:14.490
"You know, does that ever happen?"

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.790
Just kinda thinking of
the romance, and what--

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:17.910
Yeah.
What could happen at the end

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.677
and she's like, "I'm a dancer,

00:00:19.677 --> 00:00:21.820
"I'm not like, I'm not an escort."

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.627
I was like, "Oh, I'm
sorry, no, I didn't mean

00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:24.887
"to insinuate you were."

00:00:25.793 --> 00:00:28.490
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.460
Hi I'm Jennifer Lopez,
I'm one of the stars,

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.850
and producers of the movie Hustlers.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.160
And I'm Lorene Scarafia,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.020
I'm the writer-director of Hustlers.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.849
- [Both] And this is our scene breakdown.

00:00:38.849 --> 00:00:41.432
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.740
- [Ramona] Front hook, ankle hook.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.740
Now you learned all of
these moves for this,

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.840
this is--
Yes.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:53.390
Yes, this was choreographed
by Johanna Sapakie.

00:00:56.174 --> 00:00:59.257
(gentle piano music)

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.550
Hook, meat hook, hold on with that knee.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.820
- [Destiny] Okay.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.520
From here you can do the carousel.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.413
Put your head back, come down.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.110
Destiny and Ramona have
just become friends,

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:23.790
and Ramona is showing Destiny
how to conquer the pole,

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.860
and Ramona is kind of the
top money-maker of the club.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.090
- [Jennifer] She's got it all figured out.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.370
Yeah, she knows all of the moves,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.832
and she knows how to get
away with doing a lot less.

00:01:31.832 --> 00:01:33.340
(laughs)

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.363
It's like robbing a bank,
except you get the keys.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.323
Are you in?
That's the key,

00:01:40.306 --> 00:01:41.680
that's what everybody wants to know.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.890
How do I make the most money

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.490
doing the less amount of work there is?

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.618
That's right, that's the American dream.

00:01:46.618 --> 00:01:48.580
(laughing)

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.895
- [Destiny] Jesus Christ.

00:01:49.895 --> 00:01:51.880
(laughs)
Then you can go into a

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:56.513
fairy sit, (moans) stag.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.570
I want to have my heels on all the time.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.699
Can I wear my heels in this scene?

00:02:01.699 --> 00:02:04.800
Because now you feel short
instead of long and beautiful,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.633
you're like short and chunky.

00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:07.230
They're called pleasers for a reason.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.330
Yeah, when you first put them on,

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.020
it's kind of like you're a baby deer.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.280
You're walking around and you're fine,

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.870
and all of a sudden your legs give out,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.887
and you're like, "What happened?

00:02:15.887 --> 00:02:17.470
"I know how to walk in heels."

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.880
Then it becomes like,
they're ballet slippers.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.150
Then you can't do the dance without them.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.460
We shot in Show Palace
in Long Island city.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.940
This really well-run strip club that had

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.010
you know, so much space for us to work in.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.210
I know people said not to
shoot in a real strip club--

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.190
What?
But I don't think we

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.770
could have had it any other way.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.850
Oh my God it was so perfect.
I know, I know.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.680
It was really incredible, and Jane Muskie,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.100
our production designer, added
all these incredible lights,

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.830
and extended the stage,
and the owner of the club

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.850
liked it so much, he
kept everything. (laughs)

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:56.920
Did he really?
Yes, he did.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.810
Oh, I love that.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.210
Reverse stag.
That's pretty, too.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.987
Scissor sit.
Was this hard?

00:03:02.987 --> 00:03:06.450
It was very hard.
Table top.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.320
I can't do that.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.528
- [Ramona] You can do
that, you're gonna do that.

00:03:09.528 --> 00:03:10.361
(Destiny blows raspberry)

00:03:10.361 --> 00:03:14.360
A climb.
(gentle piano music)

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.600
We tried to treat it
like a stunt in a way,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.710
you know, and have as
many cameras going at one.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.120
The pole gets sweaty, it gets, you know,

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.340
you're holding it, you're
touching and you're

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.490
wrapping your body,
and you start sweating.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.190
The alcohol kind of cleans off
the pole so you can grip it,

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.770
or else you'll slip right
off and break your face.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.603
Yeah.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.570
What if you don't have muscles to do that?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.814
- [Ramona] You have muscles to do this.

00:03:37.814 --> 00:03:38.647
I don't have any.

00:03:38.647 --> 00:03:40.563
- [Ramona] Every girl
has muscles to do this.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.480
The most important thing about the scene,

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.880
and what we wanted to get was
the friendship between them,

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.930
that she became like a big sister to her.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.300
She was just like starting out,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.530
and taking her under her wing,

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:55.883
and kind of teaching her the
ropes, or the pole, perse.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.040
I wanted to make sure
that Constance, Destiny,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.390
was on stage with her, because I felt like

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:05.210
there was this scene before
where Ramona was on stage

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.980
and kind of separate from Destiny,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.380
and now Destiny's a part of this journey.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.010
I just wanted them to play
with it and keep it open.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.090
They have such a great chemistry together,

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.550
they have such a great rapport,

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:20.310
and really have this big sister,
little sister relationship.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.120
This was a beautiful scene
to kind of play that out,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.060
play out that dynamic.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.223
Their friendship is unique.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:32.140
And I love that this Chopin
piece is playing over this

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.570
to show--
You always had that.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.551
That was from the very first
script, that was in there.

00:04:35.551 --> 00:04:37.260
Yes, yeah.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.667
I remember saying, "What music is that?

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.070
"What music is that?"
Yeah.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:43.840
It just shows the grace and
the elegance of the moves,

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.250
what it takes.
Yeah, that is actually

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.960
really difficult to do these
things, and it takes skill.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.700
It's not like any person
can just jump up here--

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.770
No.
And do this.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.440
No, they're athletes, the
strength that's required

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.940
for them to do these moves,

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.570
I mean you're a dancer, of course.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.560
I had a lot of bruises and things.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.243
Yeah.
(upbeat music)

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.860
In my own dance, in her
solo kind of performance,

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:16.430
where she goes upside
down, the more really like

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:20.460
spinny stuff was harder,
climbing, things like that.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.890
We've seen a scene in a strip club

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:25.180
in every single movie and TV show ever,

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.610
and so few have been told
from the dancer's perspective,

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:31.650
so I just wanted to be in their story.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.750
So being in their story naturally
sort of lent itself to the

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.940
gaze, there's a theme of
control that runs through it.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.890
Ramona sometimes decides
what the camera's gonna do.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.812
I like to think she was
always in total control.

00:05:41.812 --> 00:05:44.050
(laughs)
She was.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:46.340
The best part of my night was to sit a man

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.570
in a bar stool and watch
Jennifer and Constance

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.740
and Kiki and Lilly sort of surround him,

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.580
and turn him into a puddle,
that was a real joy.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.910
Honestly when you bring that talented

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.540
group of women like that together,

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.410
everybody's kind of so
full of light and creative,

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.060
and happy to be there.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:06.420
You know that you're in good
company with cool people,

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.770
and you're like, this is kind of hot.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:09.770
This is gonna be a fun ride,

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.193
this is gonna be something
fun for people to watch.

00:06:12.193 --> 00:06:13.750
♪ Hot damn ♪

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.207
- [Ramona] We're family now.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:16.100
♪ Hot damn ♪

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.170
A family with money!
(ladies yelling)

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.960
From the first time I spoke to Cardi about

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.347
doing the movie, I called
her and I told her, I said,

00:06:23.347 --> 00:06:25.600
"You would know more about
this stuff than I do."

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.757
I said, "I would love to
pick your brain on what

00:06:27.757 --> 00:06:29.927
"it's really like to live in
this world, because that's

00:06:29.927 --> 00:06:32.500
"what we're trying to
capture in this movie."

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:35.700
And she definitely gave
insight into the psyche

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.480
of what goes on in an
exotic dancer's mind,

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:39.960
why they do it and things like that,

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.210
so it was really helpful.

00:06:42.877 --> 00:06:44.569
The martini.
The martini.

00:06:44.569 --> 00:06:46.319
It really does look like a martini.

00:06:51.678 --> 00:06:54.620
(laughing)

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.373
That's it, it's nothing too dramatic.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.010
Thanks for checking out
our scene breakdown.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.620
Be sure to get your tickets for Hustlers,

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.140
in theaters September 13th.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.990
You can get your tickets on Fandango.

